**Description**
I'm migrating some sync websocket code to async warp websockets and encountered a bug with some of our messages. Small messages work fine, but we have big serialized status updates of about 360 kB that when sent never arrive at the client. After this any further progress on sending messages halts and the websocket is nonfunctional.

Code is roughly this:
```rust
fn send_update(client_tx: &mpsc::UnboundedSender<ws::Message>, update: &Update) -> Result<()> {
    let dump: Vec<u8> = bincode::serialize(&update)?;
    let msg = ws::Message::binary(dump);
    client_tx.send(msg)?;
    Ok(())
}

tokio::task::spawn(async move {
    while let Some(msg) = client_rx.recv().await {
